<p>In the latest turn, Iran said it does not plan to attend a new round of talks with the United States in Pakistan on April 20. Iranian officials and state media blamed what they described as Washington’s “maximalist” or “excessive” demands and accused the US of publicly misrepresenting Tehran’s willingness to participate. The split came just as President Trump said US negotiators would travel to Islamabad to try to extend a fragile ceasefire set to expire on April 22. That keeps a diplomatic channel nominally open, even as both sides disagree over whether a second round will happen at all. Tensions also rose over dueling accounts of a maritime incident near the Gulf of Oman and the Strait of Hormuz. President Trump said a US destroyer fired on and seized an Iranian-flagged cargo ship that tried to evade a US naval blockade, while Iranian media and military-linked accounts said US forces opened fire but then withdrew after an Iranian response. The result is deep mistrust: Washington says it is still pursuing negotiations, Tehran says current conditions do not support face-to-face talks, and Pakistan remains ready to host diplomacy if the sides choose to return to the table.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/UQ5X0b-wKTjRxr0sbVTStyZwXTLmtZovh3kkKvVmAxWEcwJQsJIh3-kN0RlFOjmsS8D-FKiis6wzCoDh4AKgWE0eMUqq11iKCNANM5zJiwEk' alt='A Pakistani official is pictured during the arrival of the US Vice President JD Vance for US-Iran peace talks in Islamabad on April 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Military-led mediation: Pakistan’s effort was not just a foreign ministry initiative. Reports said civilian and military channels split roles, with Field Marshal Asim Munir carrying US proposals to Tehran during a three-day visit.</li><li>Delegation confusion: US messaging on who would lead the talks shifted, with reports naming Vice President J.D. Vance and special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner after President Trump said he would not attend, though some accounts said he might go if a deal were close.</li><li>Coercive backdrop: Trump paired the announcement of talks with renewed warnings that the U.S. could strike Iranian infrastructure if Tehran rejected what he called a &quot;fair and reasonable deal,&quot; complicating the diplomatic message.</li><li>Hormuz leverage: Several reports said the Strait of Hormuz remained all but closed or under blockade, showing how the waterway itself has become a bargaining chip in the wider confrontation.</li></ul><blockquote>We have full custody of their ship, and are seeing what’s on board! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian officials: Iranian officials said face-to-face talks cannot move ahead while Washington keeps what they called maximalist demands in place and continues a public pressure campaign over Tehran’s participation. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/iranian-official-us-maximalist-demands-stall-face-face-132163230'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: President Trump said US representatives would go to Islamabad to negotiate and framed the mission as an effort to secure a deal before the ceasefire expires. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trump-says-us-officials-will-be-in-pakistan-for-negotiations/article70880860.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistani authorities presented themselves as active facilitators, tightening security in Islamabad and coordinating preparations for another round of diplomacy despite uncertainty over Iran’s attendance. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993405/assault-on-vessel-overshadows-preparation-for-round-two-of-us-iran-dialogue'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Guardian analysis: The Guardian’s analysis argued that Tehran may see the Strait of Hormuz as strategic leverage, and that President Trump’s shifting public signals reinforce the need for a calm, tactical response. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/19/intemperate-trump-brings-chaos-and-confusion-to-iran-talks'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-news-iran-rejects-2nd-round-of-talks-with-us-excessive-demands-blame-games-11381107#publisher=newsstand'>Ceasefire Violations, Demands: Why Iran Rejected 2nd Round Of Talks With US</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-israel-war-on-iran-live-updates-strait-of-hormuz-blockade-april-20-2026/article70882986.ece'>Iran-Israel war live: Iran accuses U.S. of ceasefire breach, vows to &#x27;soon respond&#x27; after U.S. destroyer hits cargo ship</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/19/trumps-sends-delegation-to-pakistan-for-possible-new-round-of-iran-war-talks'>Tehran has ‘no plans to participate’ in new talks, state media reports, as it accuses US of violating ceasefire</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/iranian-official-us-maximalist-demands-stall-face-face-132163230'>Iranian official says US &#x27;maximalist&#x27; demands stall face-to-face talks</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0419/trump-iran-hormuz-vance'>Trump says US negotiators will have another round of talks with Iran</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/20/pakistan-ready-for-multi-day-us-iran-talks-but-tehran-unsure-about-joining'>Pakistan ready for multi-day US-Iran talks, but Tehran unsure about joining</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993405/assault-on-vessel-overshadows-preparation-for-round-two-of-us-iran-dialogue'>Assault on vessel overshadows preparation for round two of US-Iran dialogue</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/pakistans-military-chief-takes-lead-us-iran-talks-diplomatic-blitz'>Pakistan&#x27;s military chief takes lead on US-Iran talks in diplomatic blitz</a> - al-monito